From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: add document.createTreeWalker and NodeFilter, and accept URLs of any length.

Adobe's device limit page (the overactivation workflow in the IE licensing window) stayed blank. Its script walks
the page with createTreeWalker(root, NodeFilter.SHOW_ELEMENT, null, false): neither exists in Wine (documentmode.js
lists createTreeWalker for IE9+). The walker follows the DOM traversal algorithms over nsIDOMNode, with the filter as
a function or as an object with acceptNode. NodeFilter is the plain object with its constants, as on IE.
After sign-in that page's URL carries a token and is longer than 2084 characters. nsIOServiceHook_NewURI converted it
into a WCHAR[INTERNET_MAX_URL_LENGTH] on the stack; MultiByteToWideChar stopped at the end without a terminator, so
location.href ended in the saved return address and the page's encodeURIComponent threw. The buffer now fits the URL.
Test: wine/tests/treewalker/tw.html, every walk matches the DOM rules; the device page draws with its devices.

---
